<!-- ================= HOW IT WORKS ================= -->
<section id="how" class="wrap" aria-labelledby="how-h">
  <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
  <h2 class="big" id="how-h">One file goes in. It checks. Documents come out.</h2>
  <p class="lede">The package says what its documents need. <code>metais</code> holds your data to it. The golden path for using one: <strong>inspect → read → schema → validate → render</strong>.</p>

  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step">
      <div>
        <div class="no">i.</div>
        <h3>Package</h3>
        <p>A package is one <code>.metais</code> file, packed and checked by the <code>metais</code> command line tool. <code>metais pack</code> writes it after checking and testing the package; <code>metais</code> reads it in place.</p>
        <p>Inside: templates (Liquid, if you know it) that become the output files, a JSON Schema for every input, prose saying what each input means, and optionally references, assets and examples. Examples carry their expected outputs, so they double as the package's tests.</p>
        <p><strong>One package, many files.</strong> A package can declare several outputs. <code>for_each</code> makes one output per item, such as one page per article in the static-site example. And the outputs can make up a whole directory: a static site, a git repository.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
      <div class="pkg">
        <div class="parcel" aria-hidden="true"><div class="box"><div class="wax"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 14" width="26" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7.5 L6 11.5 L14 2.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div></div><div class="tag">invoice-0.1.0.metais<small>one file, packed and checked by metais</small></div></div>
        <div>
          <ul class="tree" aria-label="What the invoice package carries, from metais inspect">
            <li><span><span class="k">template</span>invoice.html.liquid</span><span class="what">becomes invoice.html</span></li>
            <li><span><span class="k">schema</span>inputs/invoice.schema.json</span><span class="what">what valid data is</span></li>
            <li><span><span class="k">guide</span>inputs/invoice.md</span><span class="what">what the input means</span></li>
            <li><span><span class="k">reference</span>references/sources.md</span><span class="what">Sources and their terms</span></li>
            <li><span><span class="k">examples</span>basic, escaped</span><span class="what">with expected outputs</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="sha">METAIS 1.0, packed, sha256:af30477b6470efed759a616226659b320d16077a474f562436f3e838c53841bf</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        <div class="fan" aria-label="One package, many files: the static-site example">
          <div class="fan-h">static-site · one package, many files</div>
          <div class="fan-row">
            <div class="fan-src"><span class="mini-parcel" aria-hidden="true"></span>static-site<br>.metais</div>
            <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            <div class="fan-outs">
              <div class="fo many-pages"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>one HTML page per article</span><b>for_each</b></div>
              <div class="fo"><i></i><span>an index</span></div>
              <div class="fo"><i class="rss"></i><span>an Atom feed</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step wide" id="check">
      <div class="intro">
        <div>
          <div class="no">ii.</div>
          <h3>Check</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="cols">
          <p>Hand it your data as files, inline JSON or <code>--set</code> flags. It reports <strong>every problem at once</strong>: the file, line and column, the JSON pointer, the field's title, the schema rule it broke, and a hint.</p>
          <p>Each finding carries a stable code, such as <code>[input.required]</code>, and the report ends by saying what to run next. Here is the invoice from fig. 1, with four mistakes in it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="proof fail" aria-labelledby="fail-cap">
        <i class="crop tl"></i><i class="crop tr"></i><i class="crop bl"></i><i class="crop br"></i>
        <div class="slug" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="reg" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/><path d="M8 0v16M0 8h16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/></svg>
          <span>Proof</span><span class="sep">/</span><span>invoice-0.1.0.metais</span><span class="sep hide-s">/</span><span class="hide-s" style="color:var(--red)">4 errors</span>
          <span class="bars"><i style="background:#14234a"></i><i style="background:#bf2f1c"></i><i style="background:#f4eddc;outline:1px solid #cfc3a6"></i><i style="background:#9a9378"></i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="fail-grid">
          <div>
            <div class="col-h"><h2>As supplied</h2><span>invoice.json · <span class="bad">4 errors</span></span></div>
<pre class="data" aria-label="invoice.json, the data as supplied, with four marked mistakes"><span class="l"><span class="ln">1</span>{<span class="ins m1" aria-label="mistake 1"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 16 L10 2 L18 16" fill="none" stroke="#bf2f1c" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span class="num">1</span></span></span><span class="l"><span class="ln">2</span>  "number": "2026-0042",</span><span class="l"><span class="ln">3</span>  "date": <span class="mk m2">"23/10/2026"<span class="num">2</span></span>,</span><span class="l"><span class="ln">4</span>  "lines": [</span><span class="l"><span class="ln">5</span>    {"description": "Consulting, October", "quantity": 12, "unit_price": <span class="mk alt m3">149.99<span class="num">3</span></span>},</span><span class="l"><span class="ln">6</span>    {"description": "Printed manuals", "quantity": <span class="mk m4">0<span class="num">4</span></span>, "unit_price": 1999}</span><span class="l"><span class="ln">7</span>  ]</span><span class="l"><span class="ln">8</span>}</span></pre>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="col-h"><h2>Proofreader's notes</h2><span>metais validate</span></div>
        <ol class="notes" aria-label="What metais validate reports">
          <li><span class="n">1</span><span class="where">invoice.json:1:1 · at /invoice/customer</span><span class="msg">Customer is required. <code>[input.required]</code></span><span class="hint">hint: Add the member `customer`.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">2</span><span class="where">invoice.json:3:11 · at /invoice/date</span><span class="msg">Invoice date is not in the date format. <code>[input.format]</code></span><span class="hint">hint: Write a value in the date format.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">3</span><span class="where">invoice.json:5:74 · at /invoice/lines/0/unit_price</span><span class="msg">Unit price in cents must be of type integer; it is of type number. <code>[input.type]</code></span><span class="hint">hint: Write a value of type integer.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">4</span><span class="where">invoice.json:6:52 · at /invoice/lines/1/quantity</span><span class="msg">Quantity must be at least 1. <code>[input.minimum]</code></span><span class="hint">hint: Write a number of at least 1.</span></li>
        </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="fig" id="fail-cap"><span><b>fig. 2</b> The marks are where <b>metais validate</b> points; the notes are what it says, word for word.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <details class="raw" open>
        <summary>The same report, as the terminal prints it</summary>
        <div class="term" role="figure" aria-label="Output of metais validate">
          <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>metais validate · the data from fig. 2</span></div>
<pre><span class="p">$</span> metais validate invoice-0.1.0.metais --data bad
<span class="loc">invoice.json:1:1:</span> <span class="err">error:</span> Customer is required. <span class="code">[input.required]</span>
<span class="dim">  at /invoice/customer (input invoice: Invoice)
  field: Customer
  rule: required in inputs/invoice.schema.json</span>
<span class="hint">  hint: Add the member `customer`.</span>
<span class="loc">invoice.json:3:11:</span> <span class="err">error:</span> Invoice date is not in the date format. <span class="code">[input.format]</span>
<span class="dim">  at /invoice/date (input invoice: Invoice)
  field: Invoice date
  rule: format at /properties/date in inputs/invoice.schema.json</span>
<span class="hint">  hint: Write a value in the date format.</span>
<span class="loc">invoice.json:5:74:</span> <span class="err">error:</span> Unit price in cents must be of type integer; it is of type number. <span class="code">[input.type]</span>
<span class="dim">  at /invoice/lines/0/unit_price (input invoice: Invoice)
  field: Unit price in cents
  rule: type at /properties/lines/items/properties/unit_price in inputs/invoice.schema.json</span>
<span class="hint">  hint: Write a value of type integer.</span>
<span class="loc">invoice.json:6:52:</span> <span class="err">error:</span> Quantity must be at least 1. <span class="code">[input.minimum]</span>
<span class="dim">  at /invoice/lines/1/quantity (input invoice: Invoice)
  field: Quantity
  rule: minimum at /properties/lines/items/properties/quantity in inputs/invoice.schema.json</span>
<span class="hint">  hint: Write a number of at least 1.</span>
<span class="err">4 errors</span>, 0 warnings, 0 info

<span class="nx">Next:</span>
  metais validate &lt;package&gt; --data &lt;data dir&gt; &lt;your --set, --set-json and --inputs-json flags&gt;  <span class="dim">— Validates the inputs again once the findings are corrected.</span>
  metais help inputs  <span class="dim">— Explains how inputs are supplied: the data directory, --inputs-json, --set and --set-json.</span></pre>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div>
        <div class="no">iii.</div>
        <h3>Render</h3>
        <p>Only checked data is filled in. Templates write any text format: for example Markdown, HTML, JSON, YAML, CSV, source code, config, Word documents, whole directories and repositories, and anything else text can be.</p>
        <p>Packages also ship static files, copied byte for byte from the package's assets: images, fonts, CSS, any binary file.</p>
        <p>Templates are side-effect free, so the same inputs always give the same bytes, on every platform.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="pair">
          <div class="term" role="figure" aria-label="The template, invoice.html.liquid">
            <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>invoice.html.liquid</span></div>
{% raw %}<pre style="font-size:12px">&lt;h1&gt;Invoice {{ inputs.invoice.number }}&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;{{ inputs.invoice.customer }}, {{ inputs.invoice.date }}&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
{%- for line in inputs.invoice.lines %}
{%- assign cents = line.quantity | times: line.unit_price %}
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;{{ line.description }}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;{{ line.quantity }}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;{{ cents | divided_by: 100.0 | amount: "USD", group: "," }}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
{%- endfor %}
&lt;/table&gt;</pre>{% endraw %}
          </div>
          <div class="mini-out" aria-label="The rendered invoice.html">
            <div class="lbl">invoice.html, rendered</div>
            <h4>Invoice 2026-0042</h4>
            <p>Northwind Traders, 2026-10-23</p>
            <table>
              <tr><td>Consulting, October</td><td>12</td><td>USD 1,800.00</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Printed manuals</td><td>3</td><td>USD 59.97</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Shipping</td><td>1</td><td>USD 8.05</td></tr>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= WHO IT'S FOR ================= -->
<section id="who" class="wrap" aria-labelledby="who-h">
  <p class="eyebrow">Four roles, four first commands</p>
  <h2 class="big" id="who-h">Who it's for</h2>
  <p class="lede">Whichever you are, <code>metais</code> tells you what it needs, and what to run next.</p>

  <div class="who">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="tagline">You've been handed a .metais file</p>
      <h3 class="cmdh"><span class="d">$</span>metais inspect</h3>
      <p>It tells you what the package makes, what it needs from you, and where to read up, straight from the file.</p>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>metais inspect · excerpt</span></div>
<pre><span class="nx">Invoice — invoice 0.1.0</span>
Renders an invoice as an HTML page, from its number, date, customer and line items.
<span class="cut">…</span>
<span class="nx">Inputs</span>
  invoice — Invoice (required; invoice.json, invoice.yaml, invoice.yml)

<span class="nx">Outputs</span>
  invoice.html ← template invoice.html.liquid
<span class="cut">…</span></pre>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <p class="tagline">You want to hand someone a template</p>
      <h3 class="cmdh"><span class="d">$</span>metais init</h3>
      <p>Write the templates, a JSON Schema and some prose for each input, and examples that prove it works. One golden path ends in a single file you can send anyone, with the rules shipped inside it.</p>
      <div class="chips" aria-label="The golden path for writing a package">
        <span>init</span><i>→</i><span class="soft">edit · render --sample</span><i>→</i><span>check</span><i>→</i><span>test</span><i>→</i><span>pack</span>
      </div>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>metais schema &lt;package&gt; invoice --fields · excerpt</span></div>
<table class="fields"><tr><td>/invoice/customer</td><td>string</td><td>required</td><td>maxLength=200 minLength=1</td><td>Customer</td></tr><tr><td>/invoice/date</td><td>string</td><td>required</td><td>format="date"</td><td>Invoice date</td></tr><tr><td>/invoice/lines/*/quantity</td><td>integer</td><td>required</td><td>maximum=10000 minimum=1</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>/invoice/lines/*/unit_price</td><td>integer</td><td>required</td><td>maximum=100000000 minimum=0</td><td>Unit price in cents</td></tr></table>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <p class="tagline">You work with a coding agent</p>
      <h3 class="cmdh"><span class="d">$</span>metais skill</h3>
      <p>It writes a SKILL.md that teaches your agent the golden paths: to <code>.claude/skills/metais/</code> for Claude Code, and to <code>.agents/skills/metais/</code> for Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor and OpenCode. Every refusal names its fix; <code>--json</code> gives any result as one versioned document.</p>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>metais skill --harness claude</span></div>
<pre>The metais skill, from metais 1.0.0:
  .claude/skills/metais/SKILL.md  <span class="ok">installed</span>  for claude, because --harness names it

A harness loads the skill when its next session starts.

<span class="nx">Next:</span>
  metais help  <span class="dim">— Lists the commands the skill teaches; a harness loads the skill at its next session.</span>

<span class="p">$</span> metais validate … --json   <span class="cut"># excerpt</span>
{<span class="code">"format":"metais.validate/1"</span>,"ok":false,"findings":[{"code":"input.required", <span class="cut">…</span></pre>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <p class="tagline">You're writing another implementation</p>
      <h3 class="cmdh"><span class="d">§</span>the spec and its schemas</h3>
      <p>METAIS is a format with a written spec, published JSON Schemas and a conformance suite. <code>metais</code> is the reference tool, not the only possible one.</p>
      <ul class="links">
        <li><a href="/spec/draft/"><span class="sec">§</span><span class="ttl">The specification, 1.0 draft</span><span class="path">/spec/draft/</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/schemas/1.0/manifest.schema.json"><span class="sec">{ }</span><span class="ttl">JSON Schemas, served at their $ids</span><span class="path">/schemas/1.0/…</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/kottera/metais"><span class="sec">✓</span><span class="ttl">The conformance suite</span><span class="path">github.com/kottera/metais</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/reference/"><span class="sec">¶</span><span class="ttl">Every command, documented</span><span class="path">/reference/</span></a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

